It seems to me that some simple rules for beginner survaval could be
collected and put into the FAQ.  These are a few I try to use (except I
usually run in hack-slash-grab mode):	

General Rule of Nethack Survival:
	He who fights and runs away will live to fight another day!

-Try not to fight more than one monster at a time.  If necessary, back
into a doorway or cul-de-sac.

-If blinded and san see nothing, find your way into a cul-de-sac (if
you already know where one is or if you can make one by pushing a rock)
and wait it out.  If you can't do that, try to find a straight passage
to wait in so that at most two baddies can get at you.  ###@###.

-While waiting, periodically step left and right (or up and down) just
in case an Eye has wandered up.  But don't wield your best weapon while
trying this.  It may be an acid blob!

-If you have speed, hit and back up.

-Don't be too brave.  Run away from superior power.  Going back up
stairs can usually help.  Note all teleport traps so as to get a free
ride away from baddies.

-Use your darts, arrows, bolts, etc. liberally.

-Pits, sleeping traps, etc. will usually affect monsters, too.  Try to
draw your attackers into them.

Here are two minor spoilers:  

-In a shop, the owner will block the door if you're holding something
unpaid-for and are close.  This can be used to create a temporary
sanctuary for healing.

-A boulder in the middle of a room can be circled to keep one monster at
bay, if necessary.

It's hard to do this without spoilers.  Do others have suggestions?
Perhaps someone could accumulate them for the future FAQ.



